In this Act:
relevant occurrence means the following:
(a) a notifiable incident;
(b) a notifiable extended absence;
(c) a notifiable suicide.

In this Act, notifiable incident means any of the
following arising from the conduct of a business
or undertaking:
(a) the death of a person;
(b) a serious injury or illness of a person;
(c) a dangerous incident;
(d) a violent incident.

The regulator may, by instrument, appoint any of
the following as an inspector:
(a) a public servant;
(b) an employee of a public authority;
(c) the holder of a statutory office;
(d) a person who is appointed as an inspector
under a corresponding WHS law;
(e) a person in a prescribed class of persons.
Note
See the jurisdictional notes in the Appendix.
